# Performance

Adapted from https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills (performance-optimization); see the
upstream skill for depth.

- **Measure before optimizing.** Don't guess hot paths; profile or reason from real data volume
  (~9M rows/yr per instrument at 1-min cadence).
- **DB:** bound every query (time window + row cap); use existing indexes
  (`idx_*_instrument_time`, BRIN on `option_snapshots.time`); avoid N+1; prefer the `metrics`
  rollup over re-aggregating raw snapshots; paginate chains.
- **API:** async I/O; connection pooling; don't serialize huge payloads — let the client request
  ranges. Consider the `metrics_5m` rollup (PRD 002/005) for long charts.
- **Frontend:** lazy-load charts; downsample series for long ranges; virtualize long tables;
  cache with TanStack Query; avoid re-fetching on every render.
- **Ingestion/insights:** fail soft, bound retries; cap LLM tool-calls/tokens; cache the static
  system prompt (Anthropic prompt caching).
- Simplicity beats premature micro-optimization — keep it readable unless a measurement says otherwise.
